message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite this archive and the datasets it analyzes."
title: "Heart rate or complexity? Analysis code for a controlled reanalysis of wearable heart rate variability in medicated inpatients with schizophrenia or bipolar disorder"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Smith
    given-names: Corbin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-1721-8640"
    email: "corbinedwardsmith@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-06"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21794970"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/corbin-smith/wearable-hrv-controlled-reanalysis"
abstract: >-
  Code and results for a controlled reanalysis of wearable heart rate variability in the open
  HRV-ACC dataset (30 medicated inpatients with schizophrenia or bipolar disorder and 30 controls,
  Polar H10), with the MIT-BIH Normal Sinus Rhythm Database as an external control cohort. Twenty-one
  HRV measures are tested against mean heart rate, recording resolution and estimator settings, and
  against movement, age, sex, diagnosis and the one recorded medication.
keywords:
  - heart rate variability
  - schizophrenia
  - bipolar disorder
  - wearable sensors
  - heart rate
  - entropy
  - spectral analysis
  - reproducibility
